.SH FILES
.TP
\fBManifest.toml\fR
Default manifest file name.
.TP
\fBManifest.<arch>.lock\fR
Default lock file name (written next to the manifest).
.TP
\fB[import].path\fR target and its matching \fI<name>.<arch>.lock\fR
When a manifest uses \fB[import]\fR, commands that load the effective package
or source universe must be able to read the imported manifest and its same-arch
lock file.
.TP
\fB[import.git]\fR
A git-sourced import stores a full URL (e.g.\& \fBhttps://host/repo\fR or
\fBssh://git@host/repo\fR) plus a resolved commit SHA and an in-repo path.
The transport is explicit in the URL and never rewritten at fetch time.
For HTTPS git, \fB[[auth]]\fR entries in \fBauth.toml\fR keyed by hostname
supply Basic/Token/Cert credentials, applied via \fBGIT_CONFIG_*\fR environment
variables so secrets never appear on argv.  SSH auth delegates to the
system \fBssh\fR (\fB~/.ssh/config\fR, ssh-agent, etc.).  To remap a URL to
a different base use git\(cqs own \fBurl.<base>.insteadOf\fR in
\fB~/.gitconfig\fR or \fBGIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL\fR.
Requires \fBgit\fR (\(>= 2.30) on \fBPATH\fR.  Bare repos are cached under
\fI<cache>/git/<sha256(url)>/repo.git\fR and partial-checkout subtrees under
\fI<cache>/git/<sha256>/revs/<sha>/\fR.
.TP
\fBauth.toml\fR
Optional auth file in the manifest directory (when \fB--auth\fR is omitted).
.TP
\fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/rdebootstrap\fR, \fB~/.cache/rdebootstrap\fR
Default cache directories.
